```

## API Endpoints

### Authentication

- `POST /v1/auth/login` - Authenticate a user
- `GET /v1/auth/verify` - Verify authentication token (protected)

### Cameras

- `GET /v1/cameras` - List all cameras (protected)
- `GET /v1/cameras/{id}` - Get a specific camera (protected)
- `POST /v1/cameras` - Create a new camera (admin only)
- `PUT /v1/cameras/{id}` - Update a camera (admin only)
- `DELETE /v1/cameras/{id}` - Delete a camera (admin only)
- `PATCH /v1/cameras/bulk-update` - Update multiple cameras (admin only)

### Other

- `GET /health` - Check if the server is running

## Authentication

The API uses JWT tokens for authentication. Include the token in the `Authorization` header:

```
Authorization: Bearer <your_jwt_token>
```

## Error Codes

| Status Code | Description                                      |
|-------------|--------------------------------------------------|
| 200         | OK - Request succeeded                           |
| 201         | Created - Resource was created                   |
| 400         | Bad Request - Invalid request data               |
| 401         | Unauthorized - Authentication required           |
| 403         | Forbidden - Insufficient permissions             |
| 404         | Not Found - Resource not found                   |
| 429         | Too Many Requests - Rate limit exceeded          |
| 500         | Internal Server Error - Server error occurred    |

## Testing All Endpoints

Below are CURL commands to test all available endpoints. You can use these commands to verify that the API is working correctly.

### Health Check

Test the health check endpoint to verify the server is running:

```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8081/health
```

Expected response:
```json
{
  "status": "ok",
  "message": "Server is running"
}
```

### Authentication

#### Login as Admin

First, login to get a JWT token:

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"username": "admin", "password": "adminpass"}'
```

Expected response:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "token": "eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9...",
    "user": {
      "id": 1,
      "username": "admin",
      "name": "Admin User",
      "role": "SuperAdmin",
      "email": "admin@example.com"
    },
    "expires_in": 86400
  }
}
```

Save the token for use in subsequent requests:
```bash
export TOKEN="eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
```

#### Login as Regular User

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"username": "user", "password": "userpass"}'
```

#### Login with Invalid Credentials

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"username": "unknown", "password": "wrongpass"}'
```

Expected response:
```json
{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Invalid username or password"
}
```

#### Verify Token

Verify the token is valid:

```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/auth/verify \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

Expected response:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "valid": true,
    "user": {
      "id": 1,
      "username": "admin",
      "name": "Admin User",
      "role": "SuperAdmin",
      "email": "admin@example.com"
    }
  }
}
```

### Camera Management

#### Get All Cameras

Get a list of all cameras:

```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

Expected response:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "data": [
      {
        "id": 101,
        "name": "Front Gate",
        "location": "Entrance",
        "active": true,
        "ip_address": "192.168.1.101",
        "port": 554,
        "last_seen": "2023-03-09T15:30:45Z"
      },
      {
        "id": 102,
        "name": "Back Gate",
        "location": "Rear Entrance",
        "active": true,
        "ip_address": "192.168.1.102",
        "port": 554,
        "last_seen": "2023-03-09T15:35:22Z"
      }
    ],
    "total": 2,
    "page": 1,
    "limit": 10
  }
}
```

#### Get All Cameras with Pagination

Get a specific page of cameras:

```bash
curl "http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras?page=1&limit=5" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

#### Get All Cameras with Filtering

Filter cameras by search term:

```bash
curl "http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras?search=Front" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

Filter cameras by active status:

```bash
curl "http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras?active=true" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

#### Get Camera by ID

Get a specific camera by ID:

```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras/101 \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

Expected response:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "id": 101,
    "name": "Front Gate",
    "location": "Entrance",
    "active": true,
    "ip_address": "192.168.1.101",
    "port": 554,
    "last_seen": "2023-03-09T15:30:45Z"
  }
}
```

#### Get Non-existent Camera

```bash
curl http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras/999 \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

Expected response:
```json
{
  "success": false,
  "error": "Camera not found with id: 999"
}
```

#### Create New Camera

Create a new camera:

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -d '{
    "name": "New Camera",
    "location": "Front Door",
    "active": true,
    "ip_address": "192.168.1.120",
    "port": 554
  }'
```

Expected response:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "id": 104,
    "name": "New Camera",
    "location": "Front Door",
    "active": true,
    "ip_address": "192.168.1.120",
    "port": 554,
    "last_seen": null
  }
}
```

#### Create Camera with Invalid Data

```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -d '{
    "name": "",
    "location": "Invalid",
    "ip_address": "invalid-ip"
  }'
```

#### Update Camera

Update an existing camera:

```bash
curl -X PUT http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras/101 \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -d '{
    "name": "Updated Front Gate",
    "active": false
  }'
```

Expected response:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "id": 101,
    "name": "Updated Front Gate",
    "location": "Entrance",
    "active": false,
    "ip_address": "192.168.1.101",
    "port": 554,
    "last_seen": "2023-03-09T15:30:45Z"
  }
}
```

#### Delete Camera

Delete a camera:

```bash
curl -X DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras/103 \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN"
```

Expected response:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "message": "Camera deleted successfully",
    "id": 103
  }
}
```

#### Bulk Update Cameras

Update multiple cameras at once:

```bash
curl -X PATCH http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras/bulk-update \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN" \
  -d '{
    "ids": [101, 102],
    "updates": {
      "active": true
    }
  }'
```

Expected response:
```json
{
  "success": true,
  "data": {
    "updated": 2,
    "cameras": [101, 102]
  }
}
```

### Testing Different User Roles

For comprehensive testing, login with different user roles and attempt operations. For example:

1. Login as regular user:
```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/auth/login \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -d '{"username": "user", "password": "userpass"}'
```

2. Save the token:
```bash
export USER_TOKEN="eyJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiIsInR5cCI6IkpXVCJ9..."
```

3. Try an admin-only operation (should fail with 403 Forbidden):
```bash
curl -X POST http://127.0.0.1:8081/v1/cameras \
  -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
  -H "Authorization: Bearer $USER_TOKEN" \
  -d '{
    "name": "New Camera",
    "location": "Front Door",
    "ip_address": "192.168.1.120",
    "port": 554
  }'
```